From ef73199aacbe259ea9b0156d81bf46d92540b813 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Pengfei Zhang <pengfei.zhang@oss.qualcomm.com>
Date: Mon, 21 Sep 2026 19:58:57 -0700
Subject: [PATCH 1/6] wifi: ath12k: Add initialization and deinitialization
 sequence for CFR module

Upstream-Status: Pending

Channel Frequency Response (CFR) module will be initialized only when
the following criteria passes:
 * Enabled CFR support for the hardware through the hardware param
   'cfr_support'
 * WMI service enabled for the CFR support
   'WMI_TLV_SERVICE_CFR_CAPTURE_SUPPORT'

Also, provide a configuration option CONFIG_ATH12K_CFR to enable CFR
feature support during the compilation time.

CFR module initialization includes Direct Buffer(DB) ring initialization
where hardware uses the DB ring buffers to copy CFR data to host.
Number of buffers and buffer size of the ring is based on the DB ring
capabilities advertised by the firmware through WMI service ready.
Also ring configurations are sent to firmware through
ath12k_dbring_wmi_cfg_setup().

Predefine ath12k_cfr_dma_hdr, ath12k_look_up_table, and ath12k_cfr
structs and fields for subsequent patches.

Tested-on: CI_WLAN.COL.1.0.c2-00317.1-QCACOLSWPL_V1_TO_SILICONZ-9
Tested-on: CI_WLAN.HMT.1.1.c7-00313.1-QCAHMTSWPL_V1.0_V2.0_SILICONZ_UPSTREAM-1

Change-Id: I533dc3030127466df606a2e3644bc0897b939c3e
Signed-off-by: Pengfei Zhang <pengfei.zhang@oss.qualcomm.com>
